---
// Privacy Notice (docs/phase-2-checklist.md Commit 6, §3/§4/§11).
//
// PROPOSED DRAFT — requires Hardcover Foundation leadership review before
// production launch. Not reviewed or approved by an attorney; nothing on
// this page should be presented to visitors as legal advice. This note is
// for the codebase only — the rendered page carries no "unapproved" banner.
//
// Describes only functionality that actually exists in this build: no
// contact form, no donation processing, no user accounts, no program
// registration, no newsletter integration, and no analytics or advertising
// integration of any kind. Do not add claims here without first adding the
// underlying feature.
import ProsePage from "../layouts/ProsePage.astro";

const email = "info@hardcoverfoundation.org";
---

<ProsePage
  title="Privacy Notice — Hardcover Foundation"
  description="How Hardcover Foundation's website handles information, in plain terms."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heroTitle="Privacy Notice"
  dek="Last updated: July 30, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This notice describes how the Hardcover Foundation website
    (hardcoverfoundation.org) currently handles information. It covers this
    website only, as it exists today.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website does not do</h2>
  <p>As of this notice, the website does not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>operate a contact form</li>
    <li>process donations or payments</li>
    <li>create or require user accounts</li>
    <li>offer online registration for programs</li>
    <li>use a newsletter or email-marketing service</li>
    <li>
      use analytics, tracking pixels, advertising cookies, or any other
      tool that profiles visitors or serves targeted advertising
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If any of these features are added in the future, this notice will be
    updated first to describe them.
  </p>

  <h2>Browsing the website</h2>
  <p>
    The website consists of ordinary linked pages. Moving between pages on
    hardcoverfoundation.org does not submit any personal information to
    Hardcover Foundation.
  </p>

  <h2>Emailing Hardcover Foundation</h2>
  <p>
    Several pages provide a <code>mailto:</code> link to {email}. Selecting
    one of these links opens the email application already configured on
    your own device — the website itself does not collect, transmit, or
    store anything you type.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you choose to send an email to {email}, any information you include —
    your name, email address, and the contents of your message — is
    provided voluntarily by you. That message is handled through your own
    email service and Hardcover Foundation's email service, the same way as
    any other email correspondence, and is not published on the website.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Hardcover Foundation takes reasonable care with the systems it controls,
    but no method of electronic communication or storage is completely
    secure, and this notice does not promise absolute security or guarantee
    against every possible risk.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Hardcover Foundation does not commit to a specific retention period for
    email correspondence in this notice. Correspondence is kept only as
    long as reasonably useful for responding to and recordkeeping of the
    inquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    This notice may be updated as the website's features or services
    change — for example, if a contact form, donation processing, or an
    analytics tool is added later. The date at the top of this page
    reflects the most recent update.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this notice can be sent to{" "}
    <a
      href={`mailto:${email}`}
      class="underline decoration-ink/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-copper-deep"
      >{email}</a
    >.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
